    {
      "receiptId": "mashed-potatoes.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Art of Cookery, Made Plain and Easy\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by Hannah Glasse, 1747 (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#glasse-1747\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EGlasse 1747\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E);",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EMashed potatoes.\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nBOIL your potatoes, peel them, and put them into a sauce-pan, mash them well; to two pounds of potatoes put a pint of milk, a little salt, stir them well together, take care they don\u0027t stick to the bottom, then take a quarter of a pound of butter, stir it in, and serve it up.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
